  "summary": [
    "C20 migrates exactly the X98 and X114 strong induced-subdivision Records and their inhabited wrappers onto GTBase.induced_subdivisions.induced_subdivision_model and induced_subdivision. The canonical keeps pattern before host, all seven fields, full sequences for every ordered pair and Prop field formulas convertible with the local copies (endpoint-inclusive induced-path match, internal-vertex conjunction, seq_consecutive, C19 raw support). The local constructor and projections remain as wrappers with identical types and implicit arguments.",
    "Seven current objects (two Records, two wrappers, the X114 decision problem, two complete rows) carry two-way cancelling transports, whole iffs and full in-NP/NP-hard witness transports. The complete rows reuse C19 X98Original (B3 path helpers, A5 subgraph relation, raw support) and X114Original (B3 path helpers, A14 maximum degree, raw support), whose certificates compile unchanged through the wrappers; all older bodies stay verbatim.",
    "The public-only client covers the empty pattern, a single pattern vertex, the identity model, a nonempty pattern against the empty host, a host edge leaving the model support and arbitrary sequences on non-edges. No reversal, off-edge, nonempty or positive-length guard is added and the interior-list Minor subdiv_model is not identified."
  ],
